# jevtrainer: goal and standing constraints

Reply to the user in Chinese. Take over and keep going; do not wait for confirmation on routine steps.

## Goal
A LLaMA-Factory-like library for Jev-style decision models (state + typed questions: choice / score / noul,
read out through a readout). Repo `C:\Users\20b90\Documents\jev\jevtrainer` (GitHub `hongliang-wei/jevtrainer`).
- Very simple, readable, modular code; easy to add datasets, benchmarks, readouts and training methods.
- LoRA and full fine-tuning now, RL later. One yaml file starts a training run (zero barrier).
- Readouts: `marker` (Intern-Decision), `slot` (BosunV3.1), `pointer` (Kev).
- Multimodal (images, now audio-video); popular and future open models must be easy to add.
- Reproduce Intern-Decision-0.8B from open data on Qwen3.5-0.8B (done, v4); then larger models and audio-video Jev.

## Standing constraints
- Open-source data only, no synthesis. No dedup for GUI data. v4 uses no GUI data beyond OneJev.
- Never write the SSH password, HF token or W&B key into a file, the repo or a logged command. They live only in
  `/root/autodl-tmp/env.sh` on the servers.
- Keep data processing going without disturbing a running training (server 2 has a 12-CPU cgroup limit:
  pin conversion jobs with `taskset -c 88-91 nice -n 19`).
- Check running trainings about every 30 minutes; on a crash restart with `resume: true`.

